    "schema": 1,
    "scope": "D3D8 standalone targets distinguish public device containers from private backing textures through an independent surface classifier. Set only after successful CreateRenderTarget/CreateDepthStencilSurface view acquisition; creation and view failures retain existing cleanup. CPU image surfaces already return devices. Preserve ordinary managed and render-target 2D/cube containers, shared parent counts, additional-buffer lifetime classification and existing NULL-output policy. The D3D8 implementation reference is DXVK, not an original Microsoft runtime; pinned Wine standalone NULL containers disagree, and direct original D3D8 HAL verification remains open. D3D9 Microsoft documentation is supporting cross-version context, not claimed as a D3D8 Windows measurement. No changes to public counts, storage lifetime, protocol, host or shader. This phase does not fix binding public-reference semantics, multiple buffers/rotation, full format/MSAA/Reset/thread/device loss, game/FPS acceptance or complete review stages 4/5/6.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "file": "d3d8-device-tests.c",
        "sha256": "f6be330259b03814f7710ad5b7aaffc60196688dca4c0ba89fb8e4241e8cdec2",
        "blobSha1": "1764980c089b2dc8d1eab36312fea856c3e59d5f",
        "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/d3d8/tests/device.c",
        "evidence": "Pinned Windows tests establish one creation-device pin for independent RT/depth/image surfaces and ordinary texture-level container identity; additional and implicit buffers return the device. These tests do not establish standalone GetContainer behavior."
      },
      {
        "file": "d3d8-container-surface.c",
        "sha256": "94409282de3533f8ddfe4392c04568346d090bb5f39f1bb33fef910613e13f89",
        "blobSha1": "5b02035d53980c006fc19122b028f9263d1219a5",
        "url": "https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/415a275e3844c252ad385b46023095e9401ca234/dlls/d3d8/surface.c",
        "evidence": "Pinned Wine standalone construction supplies a NULL container; GetContainer returns E_NOINTERFACE for it. Record this disagreement with the DXVK device-container implementation rather than calling it a native Windows oracle."
      },
      {
        "file": "dxvk8-container-subresource.h",
        "blobSha1": "06fddec3fca080ac18c91e36477af9e03eff2f4c",
        "sha256": "dbdd3307093dca709004742e89a726c5df4e241e5ae98f643331549760a21295",
